{"branch":"lang/ws-bidirectional","confidence":95,"prompt":"User says: "Lets figure out what is happening with the demo and tutorial pages. It appears that they are down on the website and I am not sure what happened to them."

Diagnosis: Caddy on the Hetzner box served blimp.bobbby.online from ~Mar 19 (TLS cert was provisioned then) until Apr 5 02:23, when a ~/code/blog/deploy.sh run rsynced the committed Caddyfile + docker-compose.yml over the top of server-local edits that had been made to add the blimp site block and volume mount. Those edits were never committed to ~/code/blog, so the next deploy wiped them. Domain has been unreachable since (TLS handshake fails because no site block exists for it).

Fix: add blimp.bobbby.online block to ~/code/blog/Caddyfile, add /opt/blimp:/srv/blimp:ro mount to ~/code/blog/docker-compose.yml (matching deciduous/phstats/donny pattern), change blimp/deploy.sh to target /opt/blimp, copy current /srv/blimp contents to /opt/blimp on server, run blog deploy, verify."}
